  "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #9937.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe public `NoInfer<T>` exported from `@tanstack/query-core` is defined as the historical pre-TS-5.4 trick:\n\n```ts\nexport type NoInfer<T> = [T][T extends any ? 0 : never]\n```\n\nWhen `T` is a generic indexed-access type (e.g. `DataTypeToEntity[DT]` inside a function generic over `DT extends keyof DataTypeToEntity`), TypeScript fails to recognize that `NoInfer<DataTypeToEntity[DT]>` and `DataTypeToEntity[DT]` are the same:\n\n```\nArgument of type 'NoInfer<DataTypeToEntity[DT]>' is not assignable to parameter of type 'DataTypeToEntity[DT]'.\n  Type '[DataTypeToEntity[DT]]' is not assignable to type 'DataTypeToEntity'.\n```\n\nThe package already requires TypeScript \u2265 5.4 (lowest CI target is `typescript@5.4`), so the built-in intrinsic `NoInfer` is available everywhere it ships.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Add a tiny `packages/query-core/src/noInfer.ts` that re-exports the built-in `NoInfer` under an `IntrinsicNoInfer<T>` alias, sidestepping the self-shadowing problem when delegating from a same-named export.\n- Change `export type NoInfer<T>` in `packages/query-core/src/types.ts` to `IntrinsicNoInfer<T>`.\n- Update `packages/vue-query/src/queryClient.ts`: `super.setQueryData<TData>(...)` forwards the `TData` generic explicitly so the stricter built-in `NoInfer<TData>` return type stays satisfied (previously the `unknown` returned from the unparameterized call was passing only because the loose tuple-index trick masked it).\n\nThe public `NoInfer` export keeps the same identity, so no consumer-visible API change.\n\n## Verification\n\nAdded type test in `packages/react-query/src/__tests__/useQuery.test-d.tsx` (`generic indexed access TData`) that mirrors the issue's repro: `useQuery` inside a function generic over `<TDataType extends DataType>` whose data is then forwarded to `getLabel(_, data: DataTypeToEntity[TDataType])`. Without the fix it errors with the exact `[DataTypeToEntity[DT]]` is not assignable message; with the fix it type-checks.\n\nLocal check matrix (all green):\n\n- `pnpm exec nx run @tanstack/query-core:test:lib`\n- `pnpm exec nx run @tanstack/query-core:test:types` (TS 5.4\u20136.0)\n- `pnpm exec nx run @tanstack/query-core:test:eslint`\n- `pnpm exec nx run @tanstack/react-query:test:lib`\n- `pnpm exec nx run @tanstack/react-query:test:types` (TS 5.4\u20136.0)\n- `pnpm exec nx run @tanstack/react-query:test:eslint`\n- `pnpm exec nx run @tanstack/vue-query:test:lib`\n- `pnpm exec nx run @tanstack/vue-query:test:types` (TS 5.4\u20136.0)\n- `pnpm exec nx run @tanstack/vue-query:test:eslint`\n- `pnpm exec nx run @tanstack/{preact,solid,svelte,angular-query-experimental,query-persist-client-core}:test:types`\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit + type tests pass on all supported TS versions\n- [x] Existing `TData should depend from only arguments, not the result` ts-expect-error test (ensures `NoInfer` still blocks reverse inference) keeps erroring\n- [x] Changeset added (`patch` for `@tanstack/query-core` and `@tanstack/vue-query`)\n\nGenerated by Ora Studio\nVibe coded by ousamabenyounes\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Replaced a custom type handling with TypeScript\u2019s built-in NoInfer to fix assignability in generic/indexed-access contexts.\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Added TypeScript-only regression tests to verify generic inference and indexed-access behavior.\n\n* **Chores**\n  * Published a patch release and added a release note documenting the fix.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---\n_Generated by Ora Studio (with Claude Code)_\n_Vibe coded by Ben Younes Ousama_\n",
